  "question": {
    "text": "Two wires of same length and thickness having specific resistances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively are connected in parallel. The effective resistivity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;cm</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math> to the nearest integer, is ___ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
